    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Clara adame\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS, INC.\n135 EAST 42nd STREET\nNEW YORK CITY\nCLARA ADAMS carried this letter\non the Inaugural Trans-Atlantic\nPassenger Flight aboard the DIXIE\nClipper - the first leg of her\nglobe girdling air trip.\nker\nPORTUGAL\n$9\n88\nFonta\n2*50 JU\nCORREIO AEREO!\nLOK20Y\nPELA\nVIA AIR MAIL\nENACAO\n*\n*\n*\nCORREO\nAEREO\n*\n*\nPAR\nFerenceLampit\nVION\n5364 sydenham\nPhila, Pa\nUSA",
      "Captaun R.o. D. Sullevan\nique Clpper, Pt Washington\n2.S.\nVIA AIR\nMAIL\n*\n*\nCORRE\nAEREO\n*\n*\nPAR\nAVION\n2000.058.1276.92",
      "PAAO\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS, INC.\nGENERAL OFFICES - CHRYSLER BUILDING - NEW YORK CITY\nClara Adams is thinking of you while\nsoaring over land and sea on her world flight.\nThe Inaugural Passenger Flight across\nthe Atlantic in the Pan American Clipper \"Dixie\"\nwas a wonderful start.\nIf all goes well, I should be back in\nNew York between July 14th and 20th.\nSincerely,\nClara Adams\nAIR ze\nMAIL",
      "PAAC l\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS, INC.\nGENERAL OFFICES - CHRYSLER BUILDING - NEW YORK CITY\nClara Adams is thinking of you while\nsoaring over land and sea on her world flight.\nThe Inaugural Passenger Flight across\nthe Atlantic in the Pan American Clipper \"Dixie\"\nwas a wonderful start.\nIt all goes well, I should be back in\nNew York between July 14th and 20th.\nSincerely.\nClara Adams\nAIR *\nMAIL"
